<title>FRANCE: Morocco buys 20,000 tonnes durum wheat.</title>
<headline>Morocco buys 20,000 tonnes durum wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco has bought 20,000 tonnes of North American durum wheat for delivery in early February at around $229 a tonne, grain traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The durum, which was bought on Monday, is likely to come from Canada, they said.</p>
<p>Morocco tendered last week for 20,000 tonnes of U.S. or Canadian durum wheat, or any combination of the two, for delivery in late January or early February.</p>
